{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/444488-gaming-convention-htr-scenario-development-need-help-please","id":444488,"title":"Gaming convention HtR scenario development: Need help, please.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T10:23:05-07:00","id":444488,"title":"Gaming convention HtR scenario development: Need help, please.","content":"I had an idea for a one-shot imbuing scenario for Hunter the Reckoning which I think would be really fun but I'm having trouble imagining some details/ending. So first of all, I guess, if you're intending to attend a Canadian gaming convention this summer and don't want spoilers for my HtR scenario... stop reading?<br /> <br /> I'm planning to promote the game as a nightschool class in bar tending. The convention promotional material would have Hunter the Reckoning as the title but then the blurb would be &quot;Welcome to KXA 101: Bar Operations. Students will learn skills in drink mixing, ...&quot; etc, the kind of thing you get in a course booklet.<br /> <br /> I would set up the scenario early and then leave. When players (&quot;students&quot;) arrive in the classroom, there would be class outlines left at the desks, nightclub music playing and a projector running.<br /> <br /> The class outlines would be a bundle of stapled photocopies including a coversheet (&quot;Welcome to KXA 101, classroom, time, teachers name...&quot; etc) a course outline, a cocktail recipe and then their character sheets with a half-page of character background.<br /> <br /> The projector would be cycling through three types of slides. The first type would be displayed for 10 seconds, it would be an advertisement for the course/school's other courses.<br /> The second type of slide would be slightly visually different, and would give players a base in the game mechanics - D10s, how to read the chara sheet, etc.<br /> The third type would just flick up on the screen for a second and it would be creepy Messenger-style messages.<br /> <br /> I would show up a little late in character as the course instructor. We would get on with the class, and our first activity would be making a cocktail. I will have cheap cocktail shakers that players would get to keep and we would each mix up a mocktail that we can all enjoy. (Gamers actually have an opportunity to learn something in my &quot;class&quot;!)<br /> <br /> OKAY SO: My story... I am a WtA player and I had this idea about the class instructor being a fomori who is using alcohol to groom this class full of humans to also become alcohol-bane fomori. A spanner is thrown in the works when the class contains a handful of pre-hunters and a mokole... I know... a mokole is a bit of a stretch, but hear me out:<br /> -I want to load up the class with other NPCs who are all dreadful WoD steroptypes- a goth, a big burly hairy guy, etc. This way players who are familiar with WoD can try and guess who the villain will be and then be surprised that the monster is a dragon but the <b>villain</b> is me, the human-looking class instructor. I think the inclusion of a dragon will completely surprise people who think they can guess the plot.<br /> -I also like that characters in WtA are not necessarily hostile towards humans or hunters.The fomori can expose the mokole who will inadvertently destroy the building and then have to deal with that.<br /> -The mokole and the fomori will fight, and the brand-newly imbued hunters will have to pick a side, or rescue bystanders in the rubble. I kind of like the idea of them being caught up in someone else's conflict. It gives players a lot of freedom to pick their actions without feeling like they have to follow my script, if you know what I mean. Actions players take will earn them an upgraded imbued character sheet with a creed/creed stats.<br /> <br /> SO: My problems: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Like I said, I want to put stereotypes in the class but I have no way for players to really interact with the NPCs to learn about them.</li> <li>I feel a little funny turning it from an immersive environment to a sit down RPG. I feel like it puts a brake on the fun. A minute ago we were all standing around chatting drinking mocktails. Now we're sitting down to RP.</li> <li>I'm not completely sold on the unrailroading. It seems a little too open. It would be nice if there was some kind of goal.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Thoughts and suggestions kindly appreciated. Peace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3798-stillawake","name":"StillAwake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}